STATEMENT: >>>
REQ-BOARD-GRAMMAR-DRIVEN carries no RELATIONS block, so the Plan tab cannot
hang it under WORK-BOARD-SHIFT even though that group's STATEMENT says it holds
it. Where it belongs is a grooming call, not a wiring fix: read as a board
consumer it hangs under WORK-BOARD-SHIFT; read as a constraint on what the
grammar layer EMITS (styles, rung semantics, a companion payload the .sgra has
no slot for) it hangs under WORK-GRAMMAR-ARCHITECTURE. Found 2026-09-01 by the
three dependency-order readers, who split 2-1 on exactly that reading.
<<<
